  "cause": "Typed field projection initialized access_size from the printed instruction suffix, using decoded operand width only for auto-update. Fixed-width bit operations had no suffix and incorrectly yielded zero in unresolved diagnostics. Multi-register diagnostics used one element rather than the whole footprint.",
  "fix": "Reuse platform_operand_memory_span for supported contiguous memory accesses, including complete MOVEM register lists and predecrement. Unsupported striped spans remain unresolved instead of scalar inference. Preserve nominal address-formation behavior. No target addresses, opcode recognizer or new flow state.",
  "contract_boundary": "Typed accesses name a starting field. An exact-start MOVEM may legitimately retain the first field symbol without proving the complete transfer fits it. field_size is a declaration size, not the transfer span. The initial proposed exact-start refusal was an incorrect test expectation, not a demonstrated framework bug; its replacement preserves that positive behavior and separately tests an interior cross-field diagnostic.",
  "regression_evidence": {
    "validated_baseline_failures": [
      "BSET missing-field diagnostic incorrectly zero width.",
      "BTST missing-field diagnostic incorrectly zero width.",
      "Predecrement MOVEM diagnostic used one LONG update instead of two.",
      "Striped MOVEP incorrectly gained a contiguous scalar-field interpretation."
    ],
    "candidate_passed": 31,
    "breakdown": {
